# Mercedes-Benz S-Class W140 saloon, 1991-1998.
#
# The "big Benz" of the 1990s: launched at Geneva in March 1991, 5,113 mm long on
# the 3,040 mm wheelbase (V140 long 5,213/3,140), 1,886 mm wide, 1,486 mm high.
# 432,732 built to 1998 (406,710 saloons); 2.8-3.2 six, 4.2-5.0 V8 and 6.0 V12.
# Facelifts in 1994 and 1996. The largest prestige saloon parc of its decade in
# Britain (22,000-29,000 licensed through the 1990s).
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercedes-Benz_W140
# https://mercedes-benz-publicarchive.com/marsClassic/en/instance/ko/220-series-S-Class-Saloons-1998---2002.xhtml?oid=453360
#
# Colours: black, brilliant silver, nautical blue and smoke silver are period
# Mercedes-Benz finishes.
#
# Weight: 20 in total (black 7, silver 6, blue 4, grey 3) against the Jaguar XJ's
# 60, matching the measured 1990s parc ratio. Provisional pending the rebase.
#
# Speed 200 km/h; comfort 170/585 (line).
# Dates: 1991-1998 with a road tail to about 2010.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/mercedes-w140.blend. References:
# citycars/references/mercedes-w140/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

